# setContext Only at Init

`experimental.async` is on. `setContext` / `runed` `Context.set` / `createX(...)` must run during first init. Calling them in `$effect`, `watch`, or after `await` throws `set_context_after_init`.

To keep children in sync when props change, **set once** and pass a **getter**. Do not re-set context.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	let { user, children }: Props = $props();

	// ✅ once at init — getter tracks later prop updates
	createUser(() => user);
</script>
```

```typescript
const context = new Context<() => User>('<user />');
export const createUser = (user: () => User) => context.set(user);
export const useUser = () => context.get()();
```

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	let { user }: Props = $props();

	// ❌ $effect re-calls setContext after init
	$effect(() => {
		createUser(user);
	});

	// ❌ await first — setContext is then "after init"
	const extra = await load();
	createUser(() => user);
</script>
```

If you need data from `await`, set context **before** the await, or move the `await` into a child that does not call `setContext`.
